    {
      "from": "杜恕（務伯）",
      "to": "廉昭",
      "type": "colleagues",
      "polarity": "negative",
      "directed": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "passageId": "ws16d-p13",
          "text": {
            "en": "Du Shu submitted a memorial remonstrating strongly against Lian Zhao, an outspoken official promoted for his abilities, urging the emperor not to let men like him sow confusion among the great ministers.",
            "zht": "杜恕上疏強烈諫止，批評因才幹受提拔的廉昭好評議時事，請求皇帝勿讓此類人攪亂大臣。",
            "zhs": "杜恕上疏强烈谏止，批评因才干受提拔的廉昭好评议时事，请求皇帝勿让此类人搅乱大臣。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "孔羨",
      "to": "司馬通",
      "type": "colleagues",
      "polarity": "negative",
      "directed": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "passageId": "ws16d-p21",
          "text": {
            "en": "Kong Xian, Colonel of the Capital, recruited the Grand General Sima Yi's arrogant and unruly younger brother Sima Tong, and the responsible officials stayed silent; Du Shu cited this as worse than yielding to private solicitation.",
            "zht": "司隸校尉孔羨辟用大將軍司馬懿驕縱不羈的弟弟司馬通，有司緘口不言；杜恕認為此事比順從私托更為惡劣。",
            "zhs": "司隶校尉孔羡辟用大将军司马懿骄纵不羁的弟弟司马通，有司缄口不言；杜恕认为此事比顺从私托更为恶劣。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
