      "to": "孟康（公休）",
      "type": "colleagues",
      "polarity": "neutral",
      "directed": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "passageId": "ws16d-p24",
          "text": {
            "en": "When Du Shu was transferred from Hongnong, Meng Kang succeeded him as Grand Administrator, governing with integrity, frugality and benevolence that won the praise of officials and people.",
            "zht": "杜恕自弘農調任後，孟康繼任太守，為政清廉簡樸、仁厚有方，官民稱頌。",
            "zhs": "杜恕自弘农调任后，孟康继任太守，为政清廉简朴、仁厚有方，官民称颂。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "程喜",
      "to": "杜恕（務伯）",
      "type": "colleagues",
      "polarity": "negative",
      "directed": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "passageId": "ws16d-p25",
          "text": {
            "en": "After Du Shu's provincial authorities executed a young attendant of a Xianbei chieftain's son without a memorial, Cheng Xi, General Who Conquers the North, impeached him; Du Shu was sentenced to death, then pardoned for his father's sake, reduced to commoner status and exiled to Zhangwu.",
            "zht": "鮮卑首領之子的隨從被幽州官府未經上奏擅自處死，北征將軍程喜彈劾杜恕，杜恕被判死罪，因其父杜畿殉職之功獲赦，廢為庶人，流放章武郡。",
            "zhs": "鲜卑首领之子的随从被幽州官府未经上奏擅自处死，北征将军程喜弹劾杜恕，杜恕被判死罪，因其父杜畿殉职之功获赦，废为庶人，流放章武郡。"
          }
        },
        {
          "passageId": "ws16d-p25",
          "text": {
            "en": "Cheng Xi had wanted Du Shu to humble himself and apologise, and when Du Shu refused he drew up a harsh indictment against him.",
            "zht": "程喜本想讓杜恕低頭謝罪，杜恕不從，他便寫下措辭嚴厲的彈劾文書。",
            "zhs": "程喜本想让杜恕低头谢罪，杜恕不从，他便写下措辞严厉的弹劾文书。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
